<article class="env-definition" id="04JY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04JY">Definition <span data-tag="04JY">66.19.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. Let $\overline{x}$ be a geometric point of $X$. The <em>stalk</em> of $\mathcal{F}$ at $\overline{x}$ is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F}_{\bar x} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{(U, \overline{u})} \mathcal{F}(U)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $(U, \overline{u})$ runs over all étale neighborhoods of $\overline{x}$ in $X$ with $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (X_{\acute{e}tale})$. </p>
</article>